"_": "portuguese-sounds.json — the table behind decks/Portuguese-Sounds-and-Spelling.folio-deck.json, read by build-portuguese-sounds.js. NOTHING IN IT IS COMPOSED. Every `like` (the English sound a letter resembles) is the 'English approximation' cell of Wikipedia's Help:IPA/Portuguese at the revision in `sources.ipa`, the European (EP) half where the cell gives two; every `ipa`, `when` and `says` is a cell, a footnote or a sentence, or a marked cut of one, of Wikipedia's 'Portuguese orthography' at the revision in `sources.orthography` — the letter table and its notes, Digraphs, Diacritics, Stress, Rhotics, Sibilants, Diphthongs and Nasalization. Wiki markup is turned into <b>, <i> and ⟨ ⟩, a link becomes its text, a footnote reference is dropped, a cut inside a passage is marked […], and nothing is reworded. `ipa` (the map at the end) is the pronunciation the English Wiktionary gives each one-word CAPLE A1 headword under the single label Portugal (kaikki.org, read 2026-11-16), copied; a word with no such transcription shows none. A row with `rx` is one the spelling decides: the builder takes its example words from CAPLE A1 in the order the deck is dealt. A row with `words` is one it does not decide (the four values of x, where the stress falls), and its words are named here. A row's `key` is what its note id is pinned to (portuguese-ids.json): never rename one.",
